Include original evidence and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new sources or places."]},"subject":"History","success_criteria":["I can use welcome with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify newcomer and explain why it matters.","I can practise include independently on a new prompt.","I can notice kindness needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Welcoming newcomers means making people feel safe and included. Actions include greeting them by their name and learning how to say it, offering a buddy, showing them around, inviting them to play, using pictures or translation to help and being patient. Supported records…","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no evidence.","Welcoming newcomers means making people feel safe and included. Actions include greeting them by their name and learning how to say it, offering a buddy, showing them around, inviting them to play, using pictures or translation to help and being patient.","A claim unrelated to the source or place."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about welcome?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample welcome plan for a new student: a buddy to meet at the gate, a map of the school with the toilets and library marked, a few words in their language if they would like to share, and an invitation to join a lunch game.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWhich are welcoming actions: asking how to say a new student''s name and practising it; ignoring them until they speak English; inviting them to join a game?\n\nFEEDBACK\nAsking how to say their name and practising it, and inviting them to join a game. Ignoring them is unwelcoming.","explain":"Welcoming newcomers means making people feel safe and included. Actions include greeting them by their name and learning how to say it, offering a buddy, showing them around, inviting them to play, using pictures or 